Build a Production-Grade, Configuration-Driven XML/ISO 20022 Flattening Engine

You are a senior Java architect and developer building a production-grade XML flattening platform for banking/payment systems.

The implementation must use Java 21, follow SOLID principles, TDD, clean architecture, secure XML-processing practices, low-memory streaming, and be safe for deployment across multiple Kubernetes pods.

Do NOT implement the whole system in one step.

Work incrementally using the development phases defined below.

---

1. Business Objective

Build a reusable Java 21 library that can flatten XML documents, especially ISO 20022 payment messages, into configurable flat records.

The library must NOT contain message-specific hardcoded parsers such as:

Pain001Parser
Pain002Parser
Pacs008Parser
Camt053Parser

Instead, users provide a YAML configuration describing:

- message name
- message version
- XML namespace
- record/repeating element
- fields to extract
- XML paths
- datatypes
- optional transformations
- optional/default values
- attributes

Example:

name: pain001_transaction

message:
  type: pain.001
  version: 001.001.13

namespace:
  prefix: iso
  uri: urn:iso:std:iso:20022:tech:xsd:pain.001.001.13

record:
  path: /Document/CstmrCdtTrfInitn/PmtInf/CdtTrfTxInf

fields:

  - name: messageId
    path: /Document/CstmrCdtTrfInitn/GrpHdr/MsgId
    type: STRING

  - name: paymentInformationId
    path: /Document/CstmrCdtTrfInitn/PmtInf/PmtInfId
    type: STRING

  - name: instructionId
    path: PmtId/InstrId
    type: STRING

  - name: endToEndId
    path: PmtId/EndToEndId
    type: STRING

  - name: creditorName
    path: Cdtr/Nm
    type: STRING

  - name: amount
    path: Amt/InstdAmt
    type: DECIMAL

  - name: currency
    path: Amt/InstdAmt/@Ccy
    type: STRING

The engine should produce one "FlatRecord" for every occurrence of the configured record path.

