2. Primary Requirements

The system must:

1. Support multiple XML message types.
2. Support multiple versions of the same message.
3. Be configuration-driven.
4. Consume XML using streaming parsing.
5. Avoid DOM parsing.
6. Avoid loading the entire XML into memory.
7. Support XML namespaces.
8. Support XML attributes.
9. Support configurable datatypes.
10. Support optional fields.
11. Support missing fields.
12. Support default values.
13. Support fallback paths.
14. Support transformations.
15. Support multiple repeating records.
16. Support inherited parent-level fields.
17. Provide a streaming record consumer API.
18. Be thread-safe.
19. Be safe to use concurrently.
20. Be safe in a multi-pod Kubernetes environment.
21. Have no shared mutable state between requests.
22. Avoid static mutable caches.
23. Validate configuration before runtime.
24. Provide meaningful errors.
25. Provide metrics.
26. Be observable.
27. Be testable.
28. Be extensible without modifying existing engine code.

Target throughput:

>= 500 XML documents/minute

Typical input:

~500 KB/XML
~1000–2000 XML lines
~20 output fields

The implementation must optimize for:

- low allocation
- low GC pressure
- predictable memory usage
- streaming I/O
- bounded concurrency
- backpressure

Do NOT optimize prematurely. Establish correctness with tests first and benchmark before making optimization decisions.

